<title>PAKISTAN: Pakistan gold price soars after devaluation.</title>
<headline>Pakistan gold price soars after devaluation.</headline>
<dateline>KARACHI, Pakistan 1996-10-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Pakistani gold prices surged 227 rupees to 5,309 rupees per 10 grams of 24-carat gold when the market re-opened on Thursday, dealers said.</p>
<p>Gold dealers had closed their shops on Tuesday and Wednesday to calculate the impact of Tuesday's 7.86-percent rupee devaluation against the dollar.</p>
<p>&quot;The sharp rise was owing to the devaluation,&quot; a dealer at the Karachi Bullion Market said.</p>
<p>($1 = 40.22 rupees)</p>
<p>-- Karachi newsroom 9221-5685192</p>
</text>
